-- title:
--   Descent of a ℓ-torsion-invariant rigidified bundle along 1×[ℓ]
-- statement:
--   Let $k$ be an algebraically closed field, $A$ a scheme with a structure morphism $f : A \to \operatorname{Spec} k$, and $L$ a relative group law on $f$: a functorial group structure on the sets of sections $\{\varphi : T \to A \mid \varphi \circ f = t\}$ for every $k$-scheme $t : T \to \operatorname{Spec} k$, compatible with base change, assumed commutative ($hc$). Assume the bundle $hA$ of properties of $f$: smooth, proper, with connected fibres, and admitting a relative group law; assume further that every fibre of $f$ has topological Krull dimension $g$. Let $\ell$ be a prime that is nonzero in $k$. Let $\mathcal Q$ be a module on $A \times_k A$ which is invertible, i.e. locally on $A\times_k A$ isomorphic to the unit module, such that the restriction of $\mathcal Q$ along the swap of the two factors followed by the slice $\operatorname{id}\times e$ at the zero $k$-point is isomorphic to the monoidal unit, and such that for every $k$-point $Q$ of the group $L(k)$ with $\ell Q = 0$ the pullback of $\mathcal Q$ along $\operatorname{id}\times T_Q$, where $T_Q$ is translation by $Q$, is isomorphic to $\mathcal Q$ (no compatibility between these isomorphisms is required). Then there exists an invertible module $\mathcal P$ on $A \times_k A$ whose pullback along $\operatorname{id}\times[\ell]$, with $[\ell]$ the $\ell$-fold sum of the identity section, is isomorphic to $\mathcal Q$.
--
--   This is the descent step for invertible modules along the finite flat surjection $\operatorname{id}\times[\ell]$ of $A\times_k A$, whose kernel pair is generated by the translations $\operatorname{id}\times T_Q$ by $\ell$-torsion points: rigidification along $\{e\}\times A$ turns the unstructured invariance isomorphisms into a cocycle, and descent data then produce the quotient bundle. It is used in the construction of the Mumford bundle underlying the Riemann form, via [`AlgebraicGeometry.RiemannForm.exists_pullback_oneProdNsmul_iso_mumfordBundle_of_forall_torsion`](thm.html#AlgebraicGeometry.RiemannForm.exists_pullback_oneProdNsmul_iso_mumfordBundle_of_forall_torsion).
